<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — Fluo"
  description="How Fluo collects, uses, and protects your personal data. Last updated November 16, 2026."
  pageTitle="Privacy Policy"
  lastUpdated="November 16, 2026"
>
  <p>
    At LinguaTech, we care deeply about your privacy. This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use, and protect your personal information in connection with the Fluo mobile application ("App"). By using Fluo, you agree to the terms of this Privacy Policy. Terms used here that are not defined have the meaning given in our <a href="/terms-of-use/">Terms of Service</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Information We Collect</h2>
  <p>We collect the following types of personal information:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Name and Email Address:</strong> Collected through Apple Sign-In or Google Sign-In to create and manage your account.</li>
    <li><strong>User ID:</strong> A unique identifier associated with your account, used internally to manage your profile and app data.</li>
    <li><strong>Purchase History:</strong> Subscription data (monthly or annual), including plan type and status, used to manage access to paid content.</li>
    <li><strong>Gameplay Content:</strong> Responses generated during language activities (e.g., dictation, quizzes, or AI conversations) are stored and analyzed to improve learning outcomes. Transcripts of AI conversations (your messages and the tutor's replies) and the feedback generated for them may also be reviewed, including with automated tools, to check the quality of the tutor and its feedback. Full conversation transcripts are kept for up to 90 days and then deleted.</li>
    <li><strong>Voice and Audio Data:</strong> Voice recordings submitted through the app are sent to our servers for transcription. Temporary audio files are deleted from your device after processing.</li>
    <li><strong>Product Interaction:</strong> Usage events (e.g., app opened, activity completed) are collected to understand general app usage and improve the experience.</li>
    <li><strong>Onboarding and First-Lesson Answers:</strong> The name you want us to call you, your goal, your level, the situations and interests you tell us about, and, optionally, your age range. They are stored in your profile and used to personalize your activities and to understand, in aggregate, who comes to the app. Only the questions the app needs to continue are required; the others, including your age range, are optional.</li>
    <li><strong>Customer Support:</strong> If you contact us, we store any details you provide in order to respond and assist you effectively.</li>
    <li><strong>Device Identifier:</strong> An identifier for your device, provided by the operating system or generated by the app, stored on your device and sent to our servers and analytics providers for analytics and account association.</li>
    <li><strong>Analytics:</strong> Device model, OS version, and usage performance metrics collected through our analytics providers to measure feature adoption and improve the experience.</li>
    <li><strong>Session Recordings:</strong> To understand how the app is used and find problems, we may record app sessions (how you navigate and what you tap on screen). Before leaving your phone, the recording hides what you type, your conversations with the tutor, your name and your email. We do not record audio or your voice. Recordings are not tied to your account (they use an anonymous identifier) and include technical device data (such as device model, operating system and app version). Recordings are kept for a limited time and are used only to find and fix usability problems.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We do not collect passwords or payment card data. Subscription payments are processed via Apple (App Store) or Google (Google Play).</p>

  <h2>2. How We Use Your Information</h2>
  <p>We use your personal data to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Authenticate and manage your user account</li>
    <li>Enable access to free or premium content</li>
    <li>Analyze usage patterns to improve features and content difficulty</li>
    <li>Process user content (such as chat messages and audio recordings) through AI service providers to enable language learning features including conversation practice, transcription, and feedback</li>
    <li>Provide customer support</li>
    <li>Monitor technical performance and usage trends</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We also use a limited set of app events to measure the performance of our own advertising campaigns, as described in Section 3. We do not use your data to show you personalized ads.</p>

  <h2>3. Advertising and Tracking</h2>
  <p>
    We do not sell your personal information or use it for data brokerage, and the Fluo app does not show ads.
  </p>
  <p>
    We advertise Fluo on third-party advertising platforms. To measure and improve the performance of these campaigns, our analytics and campaign measurement providers may share with these advertising platforms a limited set of app events (for example, app installs and in-app actions such as completing onboarding or an activity) together with device or advertising identifiers. This data is used only to measure and optimize our own ads, not to show ads inside the Fluo app.
  </p>
  <p>
    You can reset or delete your advertising ID, or limit ad tracking and ads personalization, in your device settings. Where the platform requires it (for example, App Tracking Transparency on iOS), we ask for your permission before any tracking across apps and websites owned by other companies.
  </p>

  <h2>4. How We Collect Information</h2>
  <p>We collect information:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Directly from you when you create an account or contact us</li>
    <li>Automatically through the app (e.g., device and usage data)</li>
    <li>From third-party platforms (e.g., Apple, Google) when authorized by you</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>5. Third-Party Services</h2>
  <p>
    We work with service providers that process personal data on our behalf, only to provide the services described below and in accordance with their respective data processing agreements. We group them by category; we may change the specific provider within a category, and the purposes described here still apply.
  </p>
  <p>
    User content — including chat messages and audio recordings — is sent to our servers, which act as a secure proxy to our artificial intelligence providers. These providers process the data solely to deliver the requested language learning features.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Infrastructure and database</strong> — user authentication, hosting, data storage and the servers that run the App's features.</li>
    <li><strong>Usage analytics, campaign measurement and error reporting</strong> — understanding how the App is used, measuring our ad campaigns (see Section 3), and detecting crashes and technical problems, including in our AI features. When we monitor our AI features, user identifiers and sensitive content are removed before any data is sent.</li>
    <li><strong>Session recordings</strong> — recording app sessions as described in Section 1, to find and fix usability problems.</li>
    <li><strong>Artificial intelligence</strong> — processing your text and voice for conversations with the tutor, transcription, speech synthesis, real-time voice calls, feedback, pronunciation assessment, and the quality checks described in Section 1.</li>
    <li><strong>Payments</strong> — Apple (App Store) and Google (Google Play) process subscription payments (see Section 1).</li>
    <li><strong>Advertising</strong> — the advertising platforms where we run our campaigns receive the limited app events described in Section 3, only to measure those campaigns.</li>
    <li><strong>YouTube API Services</strong> (Google LLC) — the App uses YouTube API Services to show public videos and fetch their metadata; no personal data is sent. See the <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Privacy Policy</a>.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>6. Sharing Your Information</h2>
  <p>We do not sell or rent your personal data. We only share it:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>With service providers under strict data processing agreements (e.g., for analytics or infrastructure hosting)</li>
    <li>When required by law or in legal proceedings</li>
    <li>With your consent or at your request</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>7. Data Retention</h2>
  <p>
    We retain your personal data only as long as necessary to provide the service or as required by applicable law. We initiate deletion of your personal data upon account deletion. This process completes within 30 days unless legal retention obligations apply.
  </p>
  <p>
    You may delete your account at any time from <em>Profile › Settings › Delete Account</em> inside the app.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Your Rights</h2>
  <p>
    Depending on where you live, you may have some or all of the following rights with respect to your personal data:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Access</strong> – obtain confirmation that we process your data and receive a copy.</li>
    <li><strong>Rectification</strong> – correct inaccurate or incomplete data.</li>
    <li><strong>Erasure</strong> – request deletion ("right to be forgotten") in certain circumstances.</li>
    <li><strong>Restriction</strong> – ask us to pause processing while we verify accuracy or our legal basis.</li>
    <li><strong>Portability</strong> – receive your data in a commonly used, machine-readable format and transmit it to another controller.</li>
    <li><strong>Objection</strong> – object to processing based on legitimate interests or for direct marketing.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    You also have the right to lodge a complaint with your local data-protection supervisory authority if you believe we have not handled your request properly. The <a href="https://edpb.europa.eu/about-edpb/about-edpb/members_en" target="_blank" rel="noopener">EDPB list of supervisory authorities</a> is available online.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you are a California resident, you may have additional rights under the California Privacy Rights Act (CPRA).
  </p>
  <p>
    If you are a resident of Brazil, you may have additional rights under the Lei Geral de Proteção de Dados (LGPD).
  </p>
  <p>
    If you are a resident of Argentina, you may have additional rights under Ley 25.326 (Personal Data Protection Law).
  </p>
  <p>
    If you are a resident of Mexico, Colombia or Chile, you may have additional rights under, respectively, the Ley Federal de Protección de Datos Personales en Posesión de los Particulares (including your ARCO rights), Ley 1581 de 2012, and Ley 19.628.
  </p>
  <p>
    To exercise any of these rights, please email us at <a href="mailto:contact@linguatech.app">contact@linguatech.app</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Security Measures</h2>
  <p>
    We rely on our infrastructure providers to implement industry-standard security measures including secure server infrastructure, encrypted data transmission, and access controls. While we rely on trusted third-party providers and follow best practices, no method of transmission or storage is 100% secure.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Children's Privacy</h2>
  <p>
    You must be <strong>13 years of age or older</strong>—or at least the minimum age required in your country—to use Fluo. If you are between 13 and 17, you may only use the app with the permission and supervision of a parent or legal guardian.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you tell the app that you are under 13, the app does not continue. It records only that fact, with no other data about you; from then on it stops sending usage data and deletes from your phone the answers you had given.
  </p>
  <p>
    We do not knowingly collect personal data from anyone under 13. If we discover that such information has been provided, we will delete it promptly and may suspend the associated account.
  </p>

  <h2>11. International Users</h2>
  <p>
    Your data is processed and stored in secure data centers operated by our service providers, which may be located in jurisdictions outside of your country of residence. These locations may not have the same data protection laws as your home country. By using Fluo, you consent to the transfer of your data to these jurisdictions.
  </p>

  <h2>12. Changes to This Policy</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this Privacy Policy to reflect changes in our practices or legal obligations. We will notify you of material changes through the App or by other means. The date of the last update is posted at the top of this document.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact Us</h2>
  <p>If you have any questions or concerns about this Privacy Policy, please contact us:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Email:</strong> <a href="mailto:contact@linguatech.app">contact@linguatech.app</a><br />
      <em>We usually reply within <strong>24 hours (Monday – Friday)</strong>.</em>
    </li>
  </ul>

  <p><em>We are committed to protecting your privacy and ensuring a safe user experience.</em></p>
</LegalLayout>
